ype":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"### Documentation Updates — 2026-10-14\n\nClarify two configuration contracts in the CLI and safe-output references: accepting experimental compilation notices and selecting the parent for sub-issue links. Two files changed, with no runtime changes.\n\n### Features Documented\n\n- Add `--allow-experimental` to the compile options and explain its interaction with `--dry-run`, visible notices, fatal diagnostics, and the JSON summary. Addresses the documentation portion of #68442.\n- Explain `link-sub-issue.target`: triggering issue, fixed parent, or agent-selected parent; show the explicit-parent setting and explain why scheduled/manual runs without issue context fail with the default. Based on [#68623](https://github.com/github/gh-aw/pull/68623).\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details and references</summary>\n\n### Changes Made\n\n- `docs/src/content/docs/setup/cli.md`: align with the flag declaration in `cmd/gh-aw/main.go` and the existing compilation-process reference.\n- `docs/src/content/docs/reference/safe-outputs.md`: align with the link handler and the tool schema clarified by #68623, including temporary parent IDs.\n\n### Existing Coverage\n\nRecent merged PR and commit metadata were scanned from October 13 onward, followed by targeted content checks. Retained work-queue completion (#68582), unified-session model inventories (#68600), and model-routing provider/candidate requirements (#68080, #68495) already have documentation. Existing CLI content also covers the work-queue command and Claude wizard authentication reported in #68021 and #67261.\n\nThis was a targeted documentation pass, not a detailed review of every changed file in every recent PR. Integrity-filtered results were not retrieved through alternative paths.\n\n</details>\n\n### Validation\n\n- `git diff --check` passed; only the two intended documentation files changed and the committed working tree is clean.\n- `make agent-report-progress` was attempted but stopped during the build: downloading Go 1.26.9 failed TLS certificate verification. Tests and subsequent gate checks did not run. Certificate settings were not changed.\n- No workflow source or lock changed; no workflow was dispatched.\n\n### Skipped Issues\n\n- #68442 — the missing flag documentation is addressed; the separate completion-help engine-list defect requires a CLI change, so this PR does not close the issue.\n- #51273 — host compose-stack connectivity needs a verified supported topology; no networking behavior was tested or inferred.\n- #27886 — the sandbox reference already includes Go cache paths and trust-scoping guidance; the broader checksum/restore and integrity-policy questions need further validation.\n- #67262 — per-engine timeout behavior requires additional implementation review.\n- #66978 — scaffolding parity requires product/implementation scoping; the closed not-planned issue alone is insufficient grounds to implement it.\n- #66660 — the impact claim still needs source-methodology review before revising its qualifications.\n- #66656 — the CLI reference already describes the unsupported token and wizard error; broader authentication-path behavior was not changed.\n- #67211, #66893, #66587, #66169 — existing CLI work-queue coverage addresses the repeated command gap. The experimental flag gap is covered here; runtime flag consistency remains outside these edits.\n- Additional issue results were withheld by the integrity policy and were not evaluated. The cookie-specific query returned no readable items.\n\n### Notes\n\nThe legacy `.github/instructions/documentation.instructions.md` path is absent; the current documentation skill supplied the writing conventions. `report_progress` is unavailable and was reported through `missing_tool`; publication uses the configured safe-output PR tool after a local commit. No valid steering issue number was supplied, so steering comments could not be queried.\n\nNo generic AI-coding terms were introduced or revised; AI dictionary terminology normalization was unnecessary. The protected README and documentation landing page were untouched.\n\n### Next Actions\n\nRun the repository validation gate in an environment with a working Go toolchain download, then review the two documentation clarifications.\n\n\n<!-- gh-aw-tracker-id: daily-doc-updater -->\n\n> Generated by [📝 Daily Documentation Updater](https://github.com/github/gh-aw/actions/runs/38551459107) · codex · gpt60 · 197 AIC · ⌖ 91.9 AIC · ⊞ 18.5K · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Agithub%2Fgh-aw+%22gh-aw-workflow-id%3A+daily-doc-updater%22&type=pullrequests)\n> - [x] expires <!-- gh-aw-expires: 2026-10-15T10:51:07.803Z --> on Oct 15, 2026, 2:51 AM UTC-08:00\n\n\n\n<!-- gh-aw-expires-type: pull-request -->\n\n<!-- gh-aw-workflow-id: daily-doc-updater -->\n<!-- gh-aw-workflow-call-id: github/gh-aw/daily-doc-updater -->\n\n<!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: Daily Documentation Updater, gh-aw-tracker-id: daily-doc-updater, engine: codex, model: copilot/gpt-6-astra, id: 38551459107, workflow_id: daily-doc-updater, run: https://github.com/github/gh-aw/actions/runs/38551459107 -->\n<!-- gh-aw-execution: {\"version\":1,\"repo_id\":\"1036865607\",\"repository\":\"github/gh\\u002daw\",\"aw_workflow_id\":\"daily\\u002ddoc\\u002dupdater\",\"run_id\":\"38551459107\",\"run_attempt\":\"1\",\"run_url\":\"https://github.com/github/gh\\u002daw/actions/runs/38551459107\",\"publishing_job\":{\"key\":\"safe_outputs\",\"check_run_id\":\"115813101453\"}} -->","labels":[{"id":9099894122,"node_id":"LA_kwDOPc1QR88AAAACHmVdag","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/github/gh-aw/labels/documentation","name":"documentation","description":"Improvements or additions to documentation","color":"0075ca","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":9139391526,"node_id":"LA_kwDOPc1QR88AAAACIMAMJg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/github/gh-aw/labels/automation","name":"automation","description":null,"color":"ededed","default"